The logic for the shoulder charge is primarily contained within **`components/GameCanvas.tsx`**. It is split across four specific sections within the `GameCanvas` component:

### 1. Input Detection
Inside the `update` loop, the game checks if the player is pressing the special button (Shift or 'C' or Gamepad button 7).
```typescript
const chargeRequested = !playerIsStunned && player.pushbackTimer <= 0 && (km['shift'] || km['shiftleft'] || km['shiftright'] || km['c'] || km['keyc'] || padSpecial);
```

### 2. State Activation & Resource Cost
Further down in the `update` loop, the code checks if the player has "Special Charges" (ammo for the move), is not ducking, and is not already performing an action. It sets the velocity to `CHARGE_SPEED`.
```typescript
// Special Move Initiation
if (chargeRequested && player.chargeInputReleased && !player.isCharging && !player.isUppercutting && !player.isDucking && (player.specialCharges > 0 || infinitePowerEnabled) && !isFiringFlamethrower && state.playerStunTimer <= 0 && !player.isTasing) { 
  player.chargeInputReleased = false; 
  if (!infinitePowerEnabled) player.specialCharges--; 
  player.chargeDuration = CHARGE_DURATION; 
  if (moveUp) { /* Uppercut logic... */ } 
  else { player.isCharging = true; player.vel.x = player.facing * CHARGE_SPEED; } 
} 
```

### 3. Physics & Duration
In the movement section of the `update` loop, the code overrides normal movement input while `isCharging` is true, forces the player forward, and ticks down the `chargeDuration` timer.
```typescript
} else if (player.isCharging) { 
  player.chargeDuration--; player.vel.x = player.facing * CHARGE_SPEED; 
  if (player.chargeDuration <= 0) { player.isCharging = false; if (player.isGrounded) player.vel.x = player.facing * PLAYER_SPEED; } 
}
```

### 4. Collision & Damage
Inside the enemy processing loop (`state.enemies = enemies.filter...`), there is a specific block labeled `// -- COLLISION: PLAYER CHARGE VS ENEMY --`.
*   It alters the player's hitbox to be slightly wider/shorter.
*   It checks for overlap with enemies.
*   If a hit occurs, it deals `BOSS_CHARGE_DAMAGE` (defined in `constants.ts`).
*   It applies recoil to the player (stops the charge and bounces them back).
```typescript
if (player.isCharging) damage = BOSS_CHARGE_DAMAGE;
